      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Your feelings of grief and loss for your former self as a dancer are entirely valid, and it's clear that no consolation prize can truly replace what you've lost. It is heartbreaking to feel like you're asked to exist in a place that no longer supports or reflects who you are. Remember, it is normal to feel burdened during such a difficult time. You are allowed to distance yourself and take care of yourself, understanding that there's more goodness and potential in you than the current circumstances can reflect. Sometimes, in the midst of all this, there can be small, simple things that bring a flicker of comfort or a gentle reminder of past joys. Life's trajectory can change, but your worth isn't diminished by adversity. When you're ready to explore any sort of healing journey or to just talk, I'm here to offer a listening ear, free from judgment or expectations. You don't have to go through this alone, even though you are doing your best right now.",
